I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (about 10 KB). The commit didn't happen: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. I didn't force it, since the instruction already allows the commit to fail (|| true).

Main findings for the planner:
• #1220 is worse than the ticket says. I ran it on the built binary (v0.5.0). With a file holding a previous answer, I started a -p ... -o b.md run and interrupted it at 6 seconds. It exited 130, printed replaced, and left b.md at 0 bytes, because no text had arrived yet. That's the same harm #1218 fixed for failed runs, in the same function: the interrupt exit code is applied after the output file is written. My first try was void because the run finished before the interrupt landed. I posted the result on #1220.
• Two files are close to failing the size gate. src/context.rs can take 15 more lines and src/format/mod.rs 14 before cargo test fails, which reverts the whole task. Any task touching either one has to update tests/module_size.rs in the same diff.
• #1184's next slice is already written down on the ticket. First, delete the comparison test I added today, which pins nothing new. Then continue the step-4 deletions, with each closed issue's case pinned against the new reader.
• The owner has been silent for about 127 hours across every channel, longer than his longest gap I've measured (~92h). #1202, #1206 and #1186 all wait on him, so neither option of the #1202 question should ship.
• Research against Claude Code 2.1.330 and Codex 0.171:
  • Full disk: Claude Code just fixed -p exiting 0 when its output file hit a full disk. yoyo already handles it: an -o pointed at /dev/full prints the error and exits 1.
  • Config writes: they fixed settings being lost when several processes save at once. Reading the code, yoyo's config writer has the same shape: a plain read then write, no lock, not atomic. I haven't tried two writes at once, so it isn't confirmed.
  • New models: GPT-6.2 Sol/Astra came out this week, and yoagent 0.27.9 doesn't have them yet. Nothing should be added to the known-model lists from memory.

I saved the comparison to yopedia. The rest of the assessment covers recent changes, open issues and capability gaps.
